Brothers shall fight and fell each other,
And sisters' sons shall kinship stain;
Hard it is on earth, with whoredom severe;
Axe-age, sword-age, shields are sundered,
Wind-age, wolf-age, ere the world falls;
Nor ever shall men each other spare.

- Stanza 45 from The Poetic Edda: Völuspá

The end of days are upon us my friends, and on [b]December 15th 2017[/b], you too will be tested...

